    "title": "Mexico and Belgium fight out draw in friendly at Soldier Field: Highlights",
    "text": "March 31, 2026Updated April 6, 2026, 4:18 p.m. ETMexico and Belgium played out a 1-1 draw at Soldier Field in Chicago on Tuesday, March 31 one of the teams’ final tune-up matches before this summer’s World Cup in North America.Mexico went in front within 20 minutes on Jorge Sánchez’s goal, but Belgium found the equalizer just a minute into the second half with Dodi Lukebakio’s spectacular effort.Mexico 's next match is a friendly against Ghana on May 22, followed by another against Australia at the Rose Bowl on May 30 – before kicking off the World Cup at the Estadio Azteca against South Africa on June 11. Mexico vs Belgium highlightsHere’s how the match unfolded:Buy Mexico World Cup tickets! 70th minute: Mexico 1, Belgium 1No change in the scoreline, but Mexico is pressing Belgium's back line and the physical play continues heading into the final 20 minutes. Dodi Lukebakio goal! Mexico 1, Belgium 1The Belgians equalized a minute into the second half with Dodi Lukebakio scoring a beautiful curling goal with his left foot from the edge of the penalty area.The 28-year-old scored scored two goals in last week's friendly against the USMNT. HALFTIME: Mexico 1, Belgium 0Jorge Sanchez's goal remains the difference at the half, with El Tri taking a 1-0 lead into the break at Soldier Field in Chicago.It was a chippy first half with 18 fouls between the two teams and Mexico had nine shot attempts. Jorge Sanchez goal! Mexico 1, Belgium 0Jorge Sanchez opened the scoring in the 19th minute, burying a shot into the turf off a rebound as he fell backwards, getting past goalkeeper Matz Sels. Mexico vs Belgium underway in ChicagoWe're 10 minutes into the match at Soldier Field and Mexico has looked dangerous, already managing four shots including one that required a save from Belgium goalkeeper Matz Sels. How to watch Mexico vs Belgium tonightWhen: Tuesday, March 31Where: Soldier Field (Chicago, Illinois)Time: 9 p.m. ETChannel/streaming: Fox Deportes (Watch on Fubo), ViX (Watch on Prime Video), Univision, TUDN Mexico lineup vs Belgium Belgium lineup vs Mexico tonight Mexico vs. Belgium prediction, pickDespite Mexico's clear home-field advantage in Chicago, Belgium has too much talent on paper to leave Soldier Field without securing a victory.Prediction: Mexico 1, Belgium 3",
